A table schema.sql no longer makes would lose its rows: refused.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
CREATE TABLE menu (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO menu VALUES (1, 'lunch');

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== error
table `menu` is in the database, not in schema.sql: its rows would go. Keep it, or drop it on purpose: `-- @drop 1 table menu` in schema.sql (with `-- @release 1`). Renamed? Drop it, and fill the new one from it: `-- @from 1 table <new> = menu`.
